body:
## Description

The Plan mode chat tip renders a `command:workbench.action.chat.openPlan` markdown link, but that command isn't registered in shipped builds (its implementation lives on an unmerged branch). Clicking the tip routes through `openerService` → `commandService._tryExecuteCommand`, which throws `command 'workbench.action.chat.openPlan' not found` and surfaces in error telemetry (~1,552 users on 1.131.0).

The fix is producer-side: the tip service decides which tips are eligible, so eligibility is gated on whether every `command:` link a tip renders is actually registered. A tip referencing an unregistered command is never shown, so the dead link is never presented. This is general and guards against any future stale command reference in the catalog.

- **`chatTipService.ts`** — added `_areTipCommandsRegistered(tip)`, called from `_isEligible` before returning `true`. It builds the tip message, extracts every `command:` id via the existing `extractCommandIds()` helper, and returns `false` (with a debug log) if any id is missing from `CommandsRegistry.getCommand()`. No `try/catch` is added and no `logService.error`/telemetry path is altered — an invalid tip is simply never produced. Because `registerAction2` registers into `CommandsRegistry`, real chat commands (Ask/Agent/Edit mode-open, `/init`, `/create-*`, settings, etc.) are detected as registered while the unregistered `openPlan` is excluded.

```ts
private _areTipCommandsRegistered(tip: ITipDefinition): boolean {
    const ctx: ITipBuildContext = { keybindingService: this._keybindingService, experimentalTipMessages: this._experimentalTipMessages };
    const commandIds = extractCommandIds(tip.buildMessage(ctx).value);
    for (const commandId of commandIds) {
        if (!CommandsRegistry.getCommand(commandId)) {
            this._logService.debug('#ChatTips: tip excluded because command is not registered', tip.id, commandId);
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

- **`chatTipService.test.ts`** — `setup()` now registers every `command:` link referenced by the real `TIP_CATALOG` (returned as a disposable map), simulating a running workbench where these commands exist; this keeps the existing ordering tests (which rely on real catalog tips such as `tip.planMode`) meaningful. Added a focused test that disposes the `openPlan` registration to reproduce the shipped-build state and asserts `tip.planMode` is never shown.

### Alternatives considered
- **Register a stand-in `openPlan` command** — masks the missing feature and misleads users who click it.
- **`try/catch` at `commandService._tryExecuteCommand`** — that's the crash site, not the producer, and swallowing the throw would hide errors from telemetry.
- **Remove the `tip.planMode` entry** — narrower, but doesn't cover the general class of stale references the eligibility gate handles.

